<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms it cleared Japanese/German venture.</title>
<headline>EU confirms it cleared Japanese/German venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission confirmed on Friday it has cleared the creation of a joint venture between Japanese trading company Marubeni and Germany's Hoechst Schering AgrEvo GmbH.</p>
<p>&quot;The Commission came to the conclusion that the establishment of this joint-venture does not raise competion concerns,&quot; the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;As Marubeni was not yet active in this field in Europe, the operation will not lead to the addition of market shares,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Marubeni and Hoechst Schering AgrEvo acquire joint control of the venture, to be called Marubeni AgrEvo Holding B.V.</p>
<p>The venture will be active in the field of distribution of products for the agricultural and horticultural sectors.</p>
<p>Hoechst Schering AgrEvo is itself a joint-venture of Hoechst and Schering.</p>
<p>-Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
